Hi @Kocal! Applied your suggestion in b4851401 (with the duplicated classes deduped, that was just a copy-paste artefact in the snippet — no worries 🙂).

Quick disclaimer though: thinking about it after the fact, I'm wondering if a slightly different fix would have been better. The reason `group-focus-within` was there in the first place is keyboard accessibility — combined with the `tabindex="0"` on the Trigger, it lets keyboard-only users tab onto the trigger and reveal the content. Removing it (without also removing the `tabindex`) means:

- ✅ click + mouse-away no longer leaves the card stuck open (your bug, fixed)
- ❌ keyboard users tabbing onto the trigger no longer see the content at all

If you'd rather, I can switch to one of:
- drop the `tabindex="0"` from the Trigger too, making this a hover/touch-only component (consistent, no half-broken a11y)
- or keep things as they are now and address keyboard support in a follow-up with a small Stimulus controller (the same pattern used by the other Shadcn toggle components)

Happy to do whichever you prefer! 🙏

