by Amoifr at 2026-04-26T16:16:09Z

Hi @Kocal! Done in 1c48c8ab. The new `hover_card_controller.js` toggles `data-state` on the root on `mouseenter`/`mouseleave` and the trigger wires `focus`/`blur` in addition. Both keyboard accessibility and the original click-then-leave bug are now handled. I also dropped the `group-hover/hover-card` CSS hack in favor of `in-data-[state=open]` selectors so the JS is the single source of truth.

Bonus: I added optional `openDelay` / `closeDelay` props on `<twig:HoverCard>` so consumers can tune the show/hide timing if they want — defaults to `0` for no behavior change.

Let me know what you think! 🙏

